 "methods": {
  "byteOracle": "Every cell of each EXTRAS GeoTIFF (geotiff.js) compared with the RSDMAP IMG decoded independently with DataView from its PDS3 label layout (PC_REAL, 5760 x 2880, sample centre (s+0.5)/16 deg E, line centre 90-(l+0.5)/16 deg N), after moving the GeoTIFF's -180 deg left edge to the IMG's 0 deg.",
  "loader": "The recipe's scientific block through the shared loader, sampled on an 831-point lattice including the seam and poles, compared with the IMG decode.",
  "anomalyError": "1-sigma values from RSDMAP gggrx_1200a_anomerr_l660.img read by HTTP range at each basin centre.",
  "basins": "10 km azimuthal bins around the Neumann et al. (2015) Table 1 centres; peak = highest bin inside half the central-anomaly diameter, trough = lowest bin from there to half the main-ring diameter. Neumann et al. (2015), Sci. Adv. 1:e1500852, Table 1 (https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC4646831/), used GRGM900C band-passed to degrees 6-540 with 2,500 kg/m3; this map keeps degrees 1-660 of GRGM1200A. The simple inside-minus-annulus mean contrast is also recorded; it is not their definition."
 },
